{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sullen-famished-incatern","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nAn indeterminate plan review can contain expensive successful calls plus a small retryable coverage gap. A normal rerun repeats everything, while blindly resuming old checkpoints risks applying results to changed material or policy. The maintainer approved an explicit `rebar review-plan --retry` override that resumes only the literal latest eligible review and authorizes a fresh attempt budget.\n\n## Approach\nAdd CLI parsing and a narrow library-internal retry request that reads the latest completed versioned RP-06 review journal. Eligibility requires that exact latest review to be `INDETERMINATE` with retryable missing calls. The lineage must be digest-complete and content-identical across ticket material, code/ref, effective policy, prompts/contracts, model/mode, topology, context, dependencies, and source. Legacy `REVIEW_RESULT` payloads and legacy checkpoints never seed retry.\n\nReuse every eligible successful unit, including clean and blocking results, and call only missing units. Budget-shed units remain missing. Pass-2 verification and coaching reuse unchanged per-finding successes and run only for newly recovered work; deterministic decision, assembly, signature eligibility, and narrow response rendering rerun over the combined result. Each explicit `--retry` grants a fresh per-invocation attempt budget. Cumulative lineage spend is stored as audit telemetry and never blocks a later explicit retry.\n\nFail before any model call when the latest result is not eligible or when its journal is missing, stale, corrupt, legacy, or digest-mismatched. Refusal is not a silent full review and gives the operator the normal full-review remedy. `--retry` is mutually exclusive with `--force`, `--status`, and `--check`; `--no-sign` remains compatible. Normal review behavior is unchanged without the flag.\n\nDocument the flag in the native canonical `review-plan --help`, generated `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, and `docs/exit-codes.md`. Documentation must explain eligibility, fresh budget, reused blockers/successes, zero-call refusal, incompatible flags, signing behavior, and the distinction from `--status` and `sign-review`. Review and status responses remain narrow end-result views; the retry journal is not printed.\n\n## Migration and Rollback\nThe flag is additive and opt-in. Older journals are deliberately ineligible, so rollout needs no data rewrite. Removing the CLI flag and retry reader restores full-review-only behavior while leaving reducer-ignored journals harmless. Normal review remains the documented fallback for any refusal.\n\n## Testing\nUse a real CLI subprocess with a temporary ticket store plus the production journal codec and stateful fake at the model boundary. Assert exit code, stdout/stderr contract, exact called unit ids, stored lineage, and final verdict. Fault and negative-control cases assert zero calls. A generated-help test proves the documented flag is derived from canonical help rather than hand-maintained drift.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given a literal latest completed `INDETERMINATE` RP-06 journal with two successful units and one retryable missing unit, `rebar review-plan <id> --retry` calls only the missing unit and combines all three content-identical results.\n- [ ] Clean and blocking successes are reusable, budget-shed units remain missing, verification/coaching call only for newly recovered findings, and deterministic decision/assembly reruns over the combined set.\n- [ ] Each explicit retry receives the normal fresh per-invocation attempt budget; cumulative lineage usage is recorded but never enforced as a cap.\n- [ ] A latest `PASS`/`BLOCK`, a non-retryable indeterminate result, or a missing, legacy, corrupt, stale, or digest-mismatched journal refuses before any model/provider call and never falls through to a full review.\n- [ ] CLI contract tests prove `--retry` conflicts with `--force`, `--status`, and `--check`, remains compatible with `--no-sign`, and preserves normal no-flag behavior.\n- [ ] Retry output and `review-plan --status` expose only established end-result fields and no per-unit execution trace or verbose journal details.\n- [ ] Canonical `review-plan --help`, generated CLI reference, user guide, plan-review gate guide, and exit-code guide document eligibility, fresh budget, reuse/refusal behavior, flag interactions, signing, and the normal-full-review remedy.\n- [ ] A real CLI subprocess test proves the eligible resume path, zero-call refusal path, persisted retry lineage, and final exit/verdict semantics end to end.","id":"df80-d453-2267-4953","parent_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","priority":1,"tags":["rp-06","llm","plan-review","cli","docs"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-06 S5 — Add exact review-plan retry and canonical documentation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787081121609742001,"uuid":"e2ee7a2e-879d-4006-8c01-151273a8ae9e"}